  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A reservoir releases $14$ cubic meters of water every hour. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the volume of water $V(t)$ remaining in the reservoir? Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "If the volume of water remaining is $V,$ then the rate of change of the volume is $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $14$ cubic meters of water are released each hour, the rate of change of the volume is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-14.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is negative because the volume of water is *decreasing*.",
